@host = https://localhost:7202
# After /start, copy the returned registrationId into @regId below.
@regId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 1) Start registration (Step 1: personal info). Returns { registrationId }.
### In Development the OTP is written to the console.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/registration/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-05-15",
  "zipCode": "12345",
  "email": "john.doe@gmail.com",
  "contactNumber": "123-456-7890"
}

### 1b) Resend the code (subject to the 60s cooldown + per-email cap)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/registration/otp/resend
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "registrationId": "{{regId}}"
}

### 2) Verify the OTP (use the code from the console log)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/registration/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "registrationId": "{{regId}}",
  "code": "123456"
}

### 3) Create the account (only the password — personal info comes from the session)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/registration/account
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "registrationId": "{{regId}}",
  "password": "Str0ng!Pass",
  "confirmPassword": "Str0ng!Pass"
}

### Health
GET {{host}}/health
